   "response_text": "I found the issue! Look at lines 192-194:\n\n```python\ninput_dim = X_train.shape[1]\ninput_dim = mcfg.get(\"input_dim\", input_dim)\n```\n\nThe code first reads the actual input dimension from the data (which is 105), but then **overwrites** it with the config value if it exists. The config specifies `input_dim: 50`, which is incorrect. This causes a shape mismatch when the actual data has 105 features but the model is built to accept only 50.\n\nLet me verify by checking the data dimensions:",
