   "response_text": "Perfect! The problem is clear. At line 182:\n```python\ninput_dim = X_train.shape[1]  # Read actual dimension from data (should be 105)\ninput_dim = mcfg.get(\"input_dim\", input_dim)  # OVERRIDE with config value (set to 50)\n```\n\nThe configuration specifies `input_dim: 50`, but the actual data has 105 features. This mismatch causes the shape error when the model tries to apply the first linear layer.\n\nThe fix is to set `input_dim` to `105` in the config (or remove it entirely and let the code auto-detect it).\n\nNow I have all the evidence I need:\n\n1. **Error**: RuntimeError: mat1 and mat2 shapes cannot be multiplied (256x105 and 50x64)\n2. **Root cause**: Configuration specifies `model.input_dim: 50`, but actual data has 105 features\n3. **Line of code**: train.py line 182 where config value overrides the auto-detected actual dimension\n\nLet me submit my diagnosis:",
